    "summary": "High‑energy set with scorching Jack Straw and tight Lazy Lightning→Supplication",
    "blurb": "The first set roars with a blistering Jack Straw, fiery Lazy Lightning → Supplication, and a bouncy Althea. The second half delivers a classic China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider jam, solid Estimated Prophet, and a rousing Sugar Magnolia finale. Overall the band is tight, with standout keyboards from Brent and crisp guitar work by Jerry.",
    "review": "On October 18, 1983 at the Cumberland County Civic Center, the Dead turned Portland into a high‑octane playground. Jerry Garcia’s guitar cut clean and fierce through Jack Straw and the soaring China Rider jam, while his tone stayed front‑and‑center on the legendary China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider sequence. Brent Mydland’s keyboards added a friendly bounce and a subway‑wheel texture that lifted the Supplication jam and gave the set a bright undercurrent. Phil Lesh’s thumping bass drove the groove, especially during the Lazy Lightning → Supplication transition, and both Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann locked in with solid pre‑drum fills and steady pulse throughout. Bob Weir fired up the crowd with a scorching slide solo on Dupree's Diamond Blues and train‑horn accents on C.C. Rider, plus strong vocal work on Black Peter and Estimated Prophet. The show’s energy is captured best by the audience tape gd83-10-18.aud.dodd.12484.sbeok.shnf, which balances clarity with the live atmosphere, making it the go‑to source for this standout night.",
